# sys.defined: does a name resolve as a global?
# The oracle for code that is about to be run rather than written by hand --
# an unresolved global is a fatal runtime error, so it cannot be caught after
# the fact (see the REPL in modules/web.rox).
print(defined("print"))
print(defined("len"))
print(defined("definitely_not_a_global_name"))

# A script's own top-level declarations are NOT globals -- they live in the
# script's scope, which is why a separately compiled program (a REPL line)
# cannot see them either. defined() answers for exactly the scope such a
# program gets.
var here = 1
print(defined("here"))
